        "text": "low concentrations in the feed were found to preferentially adsorb to the investigated treatment materials. Additional research is suggested to evaluate the accumulation of PFAS on treatment components to direct proper management and disposal. CRediT authorship contribution statement Nicole A. Masters: Writing \u2013 review & editing, Writing \u2013 original draft, Visualization, Methodology, Investigation, Formal analysis, Data curation, Conceptualization. Brian A. Marron: Writing \u2013 review & editing, Writing \u2013 original draft, Visualization, Investigation. Adria Lau: Investigation. Whitney G. Bailey: Writing \u2013 review & editing, Project administration, Methodology, Conceptualization. Stephen D. Richardson: Writing \u2013 review & editing, Project administration, Methodology, Funding acquisition, Conceptualization. Christopher L. Bellona: Writing \u2013 review & editing, Writing \u2013 original draft, Resources, Project administration, Methodology, Investigation, Funding acquisi - tion, Conceptualization. Declaration of competing interest The authors declare that they have no known competing financial interests or personal relationships that could have appeared to influence the work reported in this paper. Acknowledgements The authors would like to thank the contacts at AFTEC for the sup - port provided to the fieldwork team as well as the GSI fieldwork team (Alison Denn, Katie Welch, Cassidy Powell, and Sage Clay). Some of the"
      },
      {
